  "notes": "Memphis's lyric-dense narrative wing, and the only entry in this batch whose parameter set is verse-first rather than hook-first. Four things separate it from the archetype and all four come out of one fact — the loops are sampled soul and gospel rather than programmed. (1) Real harmonic motion: ii–v–i and i–iv–VII are authored as families, `maxChords` is 4, and `extensions` is seventh-weighted (0.42) with `topVoiceStepwise` true, which no other entry here does. (2) The **highest melodic note density in the modern Memphis set** — 4–8 a bar over 4- and 8-bar phrases, `emptyBarBias` down to 0.06 against the lane's 0.18. (3) The kit is deliberately plain so the lyric reads: 8th/16th hats, cowbell almost off (0–2 a bar at −6 dB), and the sparsest fill in this batch (`gapProb` 0.58, hat rolls at 0.05 a bar). (4) The verses run 24–32 bars with a short or absent hook and no beat switch (`switchUpProb` 0.02). ⛔ `low` because the research rates it medium-low: era, label and the XXL Freshman placement are sourced, **and the harmony, the drum values and the tempo band are inferences from his documented production camp** rather than from his records. ⚠ The research also says the 808 is sometimes replaced by a sampled bass line from the source record; that alternative is not modeled — the bass stays `mirror_kick` on the root at 0.8, and the sampled-bass reading would be `independent_riff`.",
